{
  "about": "Later: one list per account, which every device reads and writes in the global account data event eventType. Its content holds saved, the messages saved for later, and removed, the ones taken out of Later; each entry is room_id, event_id and ts, when it was saved or removed in milliseconds since 1970. It never holds message text. reading: the list a device takes from content. An entry without a room ID (!), an event ID ($) and a whole ts from zero to 2^53 - 1, the integers JSON holds exactly, is skipped. A message keeps only its latest entry, saved or removed, and saved wins a tie. Both lists run newest first, then by room and event ID. At most the newest 10,000 saved messages and the newest 1,000 removals are kept; a count rather than an age, so a device whose clock runs ahead can't make the others forget removals. merging: a device merges the list it holds with the account's, null when the server has none, by the same rules; it writes the result only when that differs from the account's list. setting: saving a message (saved true) or removing it (saved false) at now; the new entry lands after any the message already has, so a clock running behind can't lose the change, and a message already as asked stays as it is. An entry in saved may also hold state, archived or completed, and remind_at, when its reminder is due, in the same milliseconds; without them the message is in progress with no reminder. An older build keeps the entry and drops what it doesn't know, so it never loses a saved message. On reading, a state other than those two reads as in progress, a remind_at that isn't a whole ts is dropped, and only a message in progress keeps one. At the same moment saved beats removed, completed beats archived beats in progress, and a later reminder beats an earlier one or none, so a list an older build wrote back can't erase them. changing: marking a saved message complete, archiving it or moving it back to in progress at now, stamped as setting is; it clears the reminder, and a message not in Later, or already as asked, stays as it is. reminding: a reminder at remind_at, or null to clear it, stamped the same way; it brings the message back to in progress, saves one not in Later, and one already as asked stays as it is. tabs: In progress lists messages with a reminder first, soonest due first, then the rest newest first; Archived and Completed run newest first; a reminder due at or before now is overdue, and the message stays in progress. notifying: what a device schedules a notification for, the reminders still to come on messages in progress, soonest first, so one already due when a device learns of it doesn't notify again. presets: Remind me's choices from now in time_zone: in 20 minutes, in 1 hour, in 3 hours, tomorrow at 9:00 and the next Monday at 9:00.",
